{"id":"claim:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways--the-postpositional-adverb-eun-is-etymologically-unrelated-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways","topics":["topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways","topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways--free-verb-to-suffix"],"statement":{"en":"The postpositional adverb eun is etymologically unrelated to allative un and is likely derived from the verb un ('to fit into') with the directional/head prefix e-.","ja":"後置副詞 eun は向格助詞 un とは語源的に無関係であり、「〜にはまる」を意味する動詞 un に頭部を表す接頭辞 e- が付いたものであると考えられる。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["eun","un","e-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0301-01","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
