{"id":"claim:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways--the-ka-of-korka-can-be-analyzed-historically","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways","topics":["topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways","topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways--layering"],"statement":{"en":"The ka of korka can be analyzed historically as the restrictive postposition ka added to kor, the contemporal conjunctionalizer found in dialects such as Saru.","ja":"korka の ka は、沙流方言などに見られる同時接続語化辞 kor に限定後置詞 ka が付加されたものと解釈しうる。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["korka","kor","ka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0252-08","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways--the-nominalizing-suffix-i-and-the-construct-suffix","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways","topics":["topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways","topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways--nominalizers"],"statement":{"en":"The nominalizing suffix -i and the construct suffix -hV ~ -V(hV) in Ainu are likely to derive from the generic noun *hi.","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞化接尾辞 -i および連造形（所属形）接尾辞 -hV ~ -V(hV) は、一般名詞 *hi に由来する可能性が高い。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["-i","-hV","-V(hV)","*hi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nam2021@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways--in-all-dialects-of-ainu-the-greeting-irankarapte","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways","topics":["topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways","topic:diachrony/internal-reconstruction-and-grammaticalization-pathways--scope-tools"],"statement":{"en":"In all dialects of Ainu, the greeting irankarapte is pronounced with [ran] and never with [ram], and while it is segmentable into i-, -te, and the verb rankarap 'greet', rankarap cannot be further decomposed based on current evidence.","ja":"挨拶の irankarapte はどの方言でも [ram] ではなく [ran] と発音され、接辞 i- と -te を除いた動詞 rankarap「挨拶する」までは分析できるが、それ以上に分解することは現在のところできない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["irankarapte","rankarap","i-","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0045-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
